WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.710
Why Kiri Kiri Basara?

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.090
<i>This guy... knows about me?</i>

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.960
I've heard of you through Miyuu Aikawa.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.090
I know you also visited Seimei University
Building 10 on the day my father died.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.310
I wasn't the one who did it!
It wasn't me!

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.890
I didn't do it!

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.810
Believe me!

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.230
I didn't do... such a...

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.230
I'm not suspecting you at all.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.690
R-Really?

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.530
Tell me what you know.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.000
You're the site owner
of Kiri Kiri Basara, right?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.260
A-And you're Professor Hashigami's son?

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:17.880
Sarai Hashigami.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.350
I've posted a few comments
on Kiri Kiri Basara.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.310
Oh, right... Sarai!

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.310
SARAI!

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.190
Yes. So, I would like to confirm...

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.810
You saw the crime scene
where my father was dead, right?

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.270
Th-That's...

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.940
I told you before.
I'm not suspecting you at all.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:39.070
Because there were traces of my father
being locked up and tortured inside that room.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.660
And for you to do that, after considering
various elements, is impossible.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.160
Oh, is that right?

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.750
On the other hand,
I confirmed with Miyuu Aikawa

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.170
that you visited my father's lab
around 7 pm on February 22nd.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.300
If you saw the crime scene and then escaped,
without informing the police about it...

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.130
That's incomprehensible
and also rather unpleasant.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.100
Was there anything
that stuck on your mind? Tell me.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.720
S-Something?

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.520
Something. Because the police haven't
given me detailed information.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.270
I'm his survivor,
yet I don't know how my father died.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.230
What did you see at the crime scene?

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.860
Anything will do. Tell me something
that stuck on your mind.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:17.490
CODE.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:18.990
Code? What's that?

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:23.320
Your father wrote letters of the English
alphabet with blood on the ground.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.830
C-O-D-E.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.120
You're telling me
there was a dying message?

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.080
Y-You didn't know?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.210
The police didn't tell me
one word of that.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:31.880
Why?

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:37.090
CODE... C-O-D-E... CODE...
I've seen that somewhere.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.840
Where was it? His study? At home?

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.470
Some kind of file?

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.800
Let's look for that clue!

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:43.890
Well, but...

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.310
I beg of you! Don't you want
to find the true culprit?

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:49.390
Of course I want to do that, too!
Why was my father murdered?

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.520
But that's all useless anyway!

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.230
The day my father was murdered,

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.360
the study at home
was ransacked by someone.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.900
It's presumed that the culprit
snuck into our home

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.780
and was in the study
between 4:15 pm and 5:30 pm.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.950
That timeframe almost exactly matches
the estimated time of my father's death.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.080
This crime was completely
planned beforehand.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:10.330
Of course, all the evidence
should've been taken away!

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.210
Planned...

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:14.460
<i>How do you know there aren't
any hidden enemies out there?</i>

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.290
<i>It's not that
you're about to be roped into it...</i>

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.420
<i>You're here to become roped into it
because you want to!</i>

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.130
Even if they ransacked the place,
some evidence might still be there!

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.430
I-In any case, let's check it out!
Please take me there! I beg of you!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.180
I'm not responsible
for what happens to you.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.850
This is not a game, nor is it an anime.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.110
This way.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.780
<i>He's so surly.</i>

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.700
<i>Feels like he has a grudge against me.</i>

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.280
<i>Well, I'm sure he has a grudge
against the real culprit.</i>

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.620
<i>But it seems like he's the type
I won't get along with.</i>

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:50.500
<i>Though, you could say
Ryo-tas is my only real friend.</i>

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.790
Right now, you must be thinking
that I'm the type you dislike.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.290
No, wait—

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.090
Do you know behavioral patterns
that show up when you lie?

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.300
First, you stop making eye contact.
How about you?

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.680
You've been staring
at the bottom right of your field of vision.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.720
Second, the number of blinks decreases.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:10.020
Since we started this conversation,
18 seconds have already passed,

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.770
and surprisingly enough,
you haven't blinked once yet. Third—

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.190
Please, that's enough!

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.150
I'll be waiting here.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.150
If you want to check it out,
you go by yourself.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.240
Wh-Why?

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.950
I have yet to sort out
all of my feelings towards my father.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.740
Inevitably, my emotions get in my way.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.370
I-I've lost my father, too.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.040
What?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.040
S-So, well...

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.960
Don't think you're the only one
facing hard times.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.920
<i>That was the wrong way to say it.</i>

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.480
It's all cleaned up.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.030
There's no way to look for any clues.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.540
Key...

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:46.030
Truth is stranger than fiction, they say.
That's got to be a lie.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.990
In the real world,
miracles don't happen at all.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.460
It was too late.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.590
<i>I'm nothing more
than an ordinary person.</i>

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.260
<i>A mere high school student.
Nothing more than a NEET God.</i>

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.970
<i>There's no way I can solve crimes
like the great detectives in novels.</i>

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:16.350
I don't care.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.850
I don't care about anything anymore.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:27.440
I'd better recite the prime numbers
to calm myself down. Just kidding.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.040
Plugging up to prevent leaks in the roof.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:40.500
Nah, that can't be.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.500
This ceiling weighs in on my mind.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.630
Hello, Mr. Ceiling.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.720
You were watching what the assailant
took away from this place, right?

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:56.430
If so, tell me what that was.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.980
<i>You're already staring at the answer!</i>

00:07:58.980 --> 00:07:59.980
Wait, Zonko?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.810
<i>Why don't you notice it?
Are you an idiot?</i>

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:04.190
I don't know,
but you have a lot of static noise.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.530
But why did you choose this
as the timing for you to start talking?

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.440
<i>I don't have time to tell you the reason.</i>

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:10.610
That again?

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.870
<i>Soon, an old ghost lady
will arrive at this room.</i>

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:14.490
A ghost?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.450
<i>I was joking when I said ghost... But...</i>

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:19.950
A joke, you say?

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.040
But isn't the static getting worse?

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:24.960
<i>That old lady is the mother
of that boy with glasses.</i>

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.340
Mother? What are you talking—

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.760
<i>I'm sure she aged that much
due to anxiety.</i>

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:30.340
<i>Being so wary of others.</i>

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.630
I got proper permission from Sarai—

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:32.590
<i>Listen up, okay?</i>

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:38.680
<i>Mimicking a detective novel in real life
won't let you find anything.</i>

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:41.230
You know exactly
what was hidden in this room, right?

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:44.600
<i>There's no turning back now, so...
You have no other choice.</i>

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.070
It's okay if you speak normally!
Just give me the answer instead of hints!

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.400
<i>I told you earlier.</i>

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.280
<i>The answer is the ceiling
you're staring at.</i>

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.370
There's no way I can
figure it out with just that...

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.950
PUTTY A

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:03.250
Can it be... that these holes
in the ceiling... The professor...

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.920
Zonko! The ceiling is plugged up
in several places!

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.420
Is this the message
the professor left behind?

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.670
<i>Pretty sharp there. That's a code.</i>

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:14.180
A code? Another CODE?
This irregular array of dots?

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.680
<i>You can imagine the rest, can't you?
Don't just stand there.</i>

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:17.970
Wait, hold—

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.020
I'm not a great detective.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.190
CODE... The message
the professor left behind...

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:29.070
What are the characters he had to
leave behind in such an elaborate manner?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.150
Wait, then CODE means...

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.650
These dots are some code for characters?

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:35.660
<i>Oh, you're pretty good there!</i>

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:36.910
Wait, you're still there?

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.330
It was a mistake.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.870
It wasn't that one.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:45.920
I see.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.710
Why didn't you tell me?

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.170
Because you didn't ask.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.420
No... I guess it was jealousy.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.710
Jealousy?

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.760
A humble harassment
from a pitiful magician

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:59.100
who envies her big sister
who everyone admires.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.100
So your last name is Nishizono.

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.020
In the news...

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.270
I saw your name.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.730
So that's what that meant...

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.820
It was unexpected
that even you'd go to that side.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.700
To think that I was drawing
a picture of myself...

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.070
But in any case...

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.580
this must be the new world.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.290
March 4th (Friday)

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:30.000
<i>Molars, doujin manga,
a fortune-teller and black magic...</i>

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.380
<i>Kichijoji is full of mysteries lately.</i>

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:37.550
<i>Well, even among the mysteries from
fantasy, the card to draw in this phase...</i>

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.470
<i>has to be Kiri Kiri Basara.</i>

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:57.650
A date in a tasteful café, huh?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.660
<i>Or is there some reason
that it has to be this shop?</i>

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.040
That can't be!

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:07.660
Agent Moritsuka here.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.330
<i>Why aren't you going
after the 256 people?</i>

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.590
Are you telling me I should dance
with the ghost of Nikola Tesla?

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:16.630
In any case, the list
will connect us to those 256 people.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:19.260
<i>Do you mean that the key
was Isayuki Hashigami after all?</i>

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:22.010
That's all we have
to catch that ghost out.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.560
There's a reason for the 256 corpses,

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:28.270
and Isayuki Hashigami
knew that reason.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.900
Sarai is late!

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.150
Really.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:40.740
He said, "I figured out the mystery
of the CODE," so I'm waiting anxiously.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.870
Please give me a drink you recommend.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.170
Sure!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:00.010
Under the supervision of Myu Aikawa,
this drink has all the luckies for today.

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:01.890
This is amazing!

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.430
The visual impact sure is something!

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.390
H-He's drinking it normally...

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.060
...or not.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:12.150
Horrible! Tastes like puke!
No, really, it's horrible like puke!

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:13.690
There's zero culinary sense in this!

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.440
You'll know if you have some, too!

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.440
Try it! It's horrible like puke!

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:21.530
No, thanks. I could guess the taste
by looking at it. And I know about that series.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.410
Ryo-tas wants to try some...

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:25.620
Nothing less from you, Ryo-tas.
It's horrible like puke.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.290
What's this? I put all the luckies
for today on this,

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.960
and you say it tastes horrible?
How rude!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.500
Manager, even if
all the lucky items were on this,

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.050
this taste is already very unlucky!

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:41.170
If I were to name this...
"The Horrible Puke"!

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:44.760
No, that's not it, I need something
more dreamlike... "Fantasic Puke"!

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.680
No, I should keep in mind
its theme of lucky.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:49.270
- "Lucky Puke"!
- What happened to the "horrible"...

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.270
"Mask of Puke"!

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.480
Pukey puke!

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:54.060
What's it with all of you? Hey, Gamota...

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.770
I'm going to head upstairs,
so as punishment, watch over the shop!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.980
Ryo-tas will go with you!

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.700
You know, how you're dressed like that,
it's almost like you're Zenigata.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:08.700
- If that's cosplay, that's pretty pukey.
- Cosplay? That's something I pukey admire!

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.500
Cosplay event sites sometimes
have pukey cute girls, too.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:15.130
I've been to Comiket myself
to buy some pukey doujinshi.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.420
What are pukey ones?
Don't make it sound like they're erotic.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:20.210
By the way, this place is pukey warm
with the heating. Aren't you hot?

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.510
I'm pukey normal.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.300
If you pull out a molar by force,
it's pukey painful.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.340
Puke...

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:31.310
By the way, this isn't cosplay
but my normal work clothes.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.480
You just thought,
"Pukey horrible," didn't you?

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.610
So, I'll ask again.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.360
Have you ever pulled out a molar?

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:47.870
Police—

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:51.040
What? The fad for "pukey horrible"
is already over.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:54.540
Yuta Gamon, Seimei High School
Class 2-B, attendance number 3...

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:56.880
- Not me...
- What do you mean?

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:59.630
- It's not me!
- The conversation is pukey impossible here.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:03.760
I'm just asking whether or not
you've pulled out a molar before.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:07.590
Actually, I have to go to the dentist now
to get my wisdom teeth pulled.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.010
I'm sure it's pukey painful!

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.560
I've never liked going
to the dentist since I was a kid.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:12.220
No way.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.140
So, if you had experience
pulling molars out,

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:16.690
I thought I'd like to hear about it.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:19.940
I mean, you and I are now
Brothers of the Pukey Horrible, right?

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:24.490
I'm back, Gamotan!

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.990
Well, I need to get going soon.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.420
It was good I could have
some pukey horrible talks with you today.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.250
Oh, what's wrong, Gamota?
You're covered in sweat.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:47.220
P-o-o-l! P-o-o-l!
It's p-o-o-l! It's p-o-o-l!

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:46.170
Well, see you.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:51.510
I'm safe? Or did he let me go?

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.270
Ryo-tas...

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.230
So...

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.480
have you found any clues yet?

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.730
Yeah, I've got a lead now.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:08.700
Remember the guy in the trench coat
from the other day?

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:13.330
Because you're off guard like that,
you get framed!

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.450
I try to shut things
I'm not interested in out of my mind.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:20.460
A guy that looks like a kid,
wearing a trench coat and a felt hat.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.670
I saw that guy roaming around
in front of the shop at least twice.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:25.960
I wonder who he is.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:26.720
Who knows?

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.970
But it's for certain
that he's up to something.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:33.680
I saw him earlier and was observing him.
He met some unexpected people.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:34.600
Unexpected people?

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:39.310
You remember the two high school girls
who requested a devil ritual, right?

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:41.310
I was following the guy
in the trench coat

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:44.980
when one of the two girls, the little wench
with the huge knockers, showed up.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.360
What a crass way of saying it.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:48.570
But that's not all.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:52.370
The two-timing guy who the little wench
asked to have cursed was with her, too.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:56.160
The client, the target of the curse
and a shady guy who was roaming around...

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.160
All of them entered,
then left the exact same location.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.670
The place was called Café Blue Moon.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:01.580
Wasn't it coincidence?

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.670
And that's why
people make a fool of you.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:05.420
There were no other customers
in that café.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.460
The three were talking about something,

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.630
all with ominous-looking
expressions on their faces.

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:13.430
There's no doubt they've grouped up
to sniff around what we've been doing.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.970
If they're trying to know
of the existence of devils,

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.480
we must take the appropriate
countermeasures, as well.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:22.310
If they're out to get us, let's set
something up against them instead.

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:26.900
In any case, I hear your voice
unusually clearly today.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.690
Well, that's not a surprise,

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:31.200
given how the situation changes.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:35.580
Hello there.
Can I have a quick word with you?

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:36.410
And you are?

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.910
The much-rumored detective.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:40.290
I'd like to ask you
about Professor Hashigami.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:52.630
SARAI is... pitiful... a pitiful person!

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:57.140
You're late. Hurry up and tell me
the mystery of the CODE.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:58.100
Guys...

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:01.810
if there are four of you gathered up,
can you at least order something?

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.020
Anyway, the mystery! Hurry!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:10.320
In short, the CODE is characters that have
been encrypted using the Baudot Code.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.490
These characters were crammed up
all over the ceiling.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:15.160
That's what I came up with!

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.830
That's something
even Zonko complimented me on!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.950
Gamo-senpai, that's amazing!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:20.790
What's Zonko?

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.790
This radio is Zonko.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.540
What are you talking about?

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.840
This talks quite a bit.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.460
Gamo-senpai,
there you go with that again!

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:33.470
And, what kind of characters
were written on the ceiling?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.720
People's names.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.550
Can it be Ririka Nishizono?

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.810
- Who's that?
- Oh, it wasn't?

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.430
It wasn't just one particular person.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.350
It was the names for...

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:44.310
256 people.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.980
Those 256 people...

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:54.030
no matter how you think about it...
is from you-know-what?

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:54.780
Yeah.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:58.240
This may be the list of the victims
who were found in Inokashira Park.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:02.080
U-Um, was the name Chizu Kawabata
one of the names on that list?

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.120
Someone you know?

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.040
Yes. She's a close friend.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:06.920
I haven't confirmed that name.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:10.130
It'll take quite a long time
to decipher every name.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:13.840
And I focused on the deciphering
of a more perplexing string of characters.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:15.430
A perplexing string of characters?

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:18.640
Yeah. There was a cryptic
ten-character string

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:22.470
attached at the end of each name
for these 256 people, like it was part of a set.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.480
I couldn't find the answer
for what that was.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:28.150
Did those ten characters at the end
have some sort of a pattern?

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:30.820
Of the ten characters,
the last seven digits were standardized.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.780
They were "EEQTUWI."

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:36.070
The three digits before that change.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.990
By the way, Sarai,

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:41.410
have you checked
any of the victims' names from the news?

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.580
No, not yet.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:46.330
The names I deciphered were only
about ten of those I randomly chose.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.500
Then, Ryo-tas,
thanks for deciphering this.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.500
Ryo-tas? Yeah, sure.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:54.050
I'm totally airheaded,
so you can leave it all to me!

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:54.800
Jeez.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:02.310
By the way, you mentioned
the name Ririka Nishizono earlier.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.560
Who's that?

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:08.270
The person I thought
might be the true culprit.

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.810
The true culprit? Who is she?

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.230
An adult doujin artist.

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:13.110
What was that?

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:14.150
The author who drew this.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.860
A DARK WATER'S BOTTOM

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.070
You know, can I go home now?

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:18.820
Wait, hold it! I have a reason for this!

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.120
There's advance announcement
of Professor Hashigami's murder in here!

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:24.040
Right here! This guy was murdered,
and his tooth was gouged out, right?

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.950
This is advance announcement
of my father's murder?

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:29.420
Are you saying this is a prediction
with this level of congruence?

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:31.790
No, that's not it!
That's not all! Look here!

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:34.250
The object the dead guy is pointing to!

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:35.380
- CODE...
- Right.

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:38.970
The same dying message as the one
Professor Hashigami left at the crime scene!

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:41.340
Only a few people know about this!

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:44.680
And this doujinshi was published
for last year's winter Comiket!

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:45.890
You get the rest, right?

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:48.770
Gamo-senpai, I'm sorry to interrupt
while you have this look of self-satisfaction,

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:50.190
but isn't that just a coincidence?

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.110
Probably a coincidence.
CODE is a commonplace word,

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.230
and this alone is very weak as evidence.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:57.190
There needs to be at least
three points of congruence

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:59.030
for a coincidence to become a necessity.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.410
At least three...

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.830
I-In any case, at least read
the contents properly once... please.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.460
Are you asserting synchronicity?

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.050
The world is full of coincidences.

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:20.090
And yet, as a result of trying to give meaning
to everything, conspiracy theories are born.

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.050
Is that so?

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:25.930
I'm sure conspiracies exist in this world.
It's more fun to believe they do.

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:31.560
But you can't deny that people clamoring
conspiracy theories are illogical, right?

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:35.820
They also put aside the parts
that are inconvenient for them.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:38.820
Wait a minute. This... This number...

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.280
3315728? Is something wrong about this?

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.910
I see... I see...
So that's what it means!

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.530
Sarai! Explain it to us!

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:48.620
"EEQTUWI."

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.370
This is the "EEQTUWI"
that I couldn't decipher!

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:56.800
In the Baudot Code, you can encrypt
numbers as well as letters of the alphabet!

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:00.670
According to the character code conversion
table, E becomes 3, and Q becomes 1.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:03.180
- It can't be!
- 3315728.

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:05.180
It's the same as this license plate!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.930
The same as the message
left behind by Professor Hashigami!

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:10.930
So Ririka Nishizono might be
the real culprit, right?

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:11.940
Gamon, I'm sorry.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.730
I think I'll dig deeper
into this case in my own way.

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:18.110
And were there any other accounts
that are stuck on your mind?

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:19.610
Let's see...

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.360
What are you hiding?

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:22.490
Wh-What?

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:25.120
For a while, you haven't tried
to make eye contact as you speak.

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.200
You keep asking back, "What?"

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:29.330
That's proof that you're pretending
you don't know anything

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.870
while recognizing the material
you're being questioned about.

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.790
Is there something you're ashamed of?

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.710
Th-This...

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.210
I-Is something wrong?

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:39.250
Kotori... Kotoriba... No, that's not it.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.420
Kotoribako...

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.850
Do you know of Frankenstein?

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:53.390
The story where they gathered
parts from cadavers

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.650
and stitched them together
in hopes of creating a human.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:59.020
But it lacked a critical component,
the soul, and it turned into a monster.

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:04.900
I wonder if you can
stitch a soul together, as well.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:07.280
And if so, what in the world
will be created?
